<title>USA: Old Republic International may issue notes.</title>
<headline>Old Republic International may issue notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Old Republic International Corp is expected to issue $115 million in 10-year notes, according to market sources.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers is expected to serve as the lead manager for the offering, they added.</p>
<p>The non-callable notes are expected to be rated Aa3/AA-minus and has price talk of +60 basis points over U.S. Treasuries, sources added.</p>
<p>Old Republic provides risk management and reinsurance services in the property/casualty, title, mortgage guaranty, life and health fields.</p>
<p>((- Caryn Trokie, 212-859-1678 -))</p>
